          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जेबकतरा — jebkatrā — \"a pickpocket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बाज़ार में एक जेबकतरा घूम रहा था। bāzār meṁ ek jebkatrā ghūm rahā thā. A pickpocket was wandering through the market."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जेबकतरा (jebkatrā) is जेब, a pocket, and katrā, one who snips, from katarnā, to clip, which CDIAL 2858 lists for Hindi under Sanskrit kartarī, \"scissors\": the one who cuts into pockets."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
